          "text": "Now let me do a final spec compliance check. Comparing the implementation against every spec requirement:\n\n**Spec §2.1 — SendStream method:**\n- Request construction identical to `Send()` with `Stream: true` ✅\n- Same endpoint, same headers ✅\n- Non-2xx: read body, close, return `handleErrorResponse()` ✅\n- 2xx: wrap in `EventStream`, don't close body ✅\n- Context cancellation → `ErrCategoryTimeout` ✅\n\n**Spec §2.2 — SSE-to-StreamEvent mapping:**\n- `message_start` → store inputTokens, no event ✅\n- `content_block_start` text → store block, no event ✅\n- `content_block_start` tool_use → `StreamEventToolStart` ✅\n- `text_delta` → `StreamEventText` ✅\n- `input_json_delta` → `StreamEventToolDelta` with ToolCallID lookup ✅\n- `content_block_stop` text → no event ✅\n- `content_block_stop` tool_use → `StreamEventToolEnd` ✅\n- `message_delta` → `StreamEventDone` with tokens/stop_reason ✅\n- `message_stop` → `io.EOF` ✅\n- `ping` → skip ✅\n- `error` → `ProviderError` via `mapStreamErrorType` ✅\n- Closure state: `inputTokens int`, `blocks map[int]blockInfo` ✅\n\n**Spec §2.3 — Wire format types:** All structs present ✅\n\n**Spec §2.4 — Edge cases:** All 10 edge cases covered with tests ✅\n\n**Spec §2.5 — Code reuse:**\n- `convertToAnthropicMessages()` ✅\n- `convertToAnthropicTools()` ✅\n- `handleErrorResponse()` ✅\n- `NewSSEParser()` ✅\n- `NewEventStream()` ✅\n- `anthropicRequest` extended with `Stream` field ✅\n\nAll spec requirements are met. Let me verify the full build compiles:",
